    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.45, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"wrong_rating\", \"components\": [\"U4\"], \"pins\": [\"U4.5\", \"U4.3\"], \"nets\": [\"VCC\", \"SDA\", \"Net-(U4-Pad2)\"], \"observed\": \"U4 (74LVC1G34) has its VCC pin (pin 5) on net VCC, the same rail that feeds the input of the LM1117-5.0 regulator U1 (VI, pin 3) and the PMOS-switched fan supply. That rail is above 5 V, since the LM1117-5.0 needs more than 6.5 V at its input to regulate, and the fan supply is switched from it. U4's output (pin 4) drives SDA, which is shared with the 5 V ATtiny45 and the ISP MOSI pin.\", \"expected\": \"A 74LVC1G34 is a 1.65\u20135.5 V logic buffer and should be powered from the regulated +5V rail (or the same rail as the logic it interfaces with), not from the unregulated VCC supply that may be 12 V.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U4\\\") (pin \\\"5\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCC\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"3\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VI\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VO\\\") (pintype \\\"power_out\\\"))\"}], \"impact\": \"If VCC is the higher fan supply, U4 is overvoltage-stressed and may be destroyed. Its output would also drive SDA at the wrong logic level, which can cause incorrect behaviour on the shared line.\", \"confidence\": 0.4}, {\"category\": \"wrong_value\", \"components\": [\"C2\", \"U1\"], \"pins\": [\"C2.1\", \"U1.2\"], \"nets\": [\"+5V\"], \"observed\": \"The only output capacitor on the LM1117-5.0 regulator output (+5V) is C2, a 100nF 0805 ceramic.\", \"expected\": \"The LM1117 datasheet requires an output capacitor of roughly 10 \u00b5F (tantalum or aluminium electrolytic, with ESR limits) for stability. A 100nF ceramic alone is not sufficient for stable regulation.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"C2\\\") (value \\\"100nF\\\") (footprint \\\"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"C2\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}], \"impact\": \"The regulator may oscillate or be unstable under load, causing the +5V rail to be noisy or unreliable for the ATtiny45, ATtiny13 and fan-connector logic.\", \"confidence\": 0.25}]], \"summary\": \"The netlist does not match the repo spec, which does not describe this fan controller, so the verdict relies on electrical practice. The most likely problem is the 74LVC1G34 buffer U4 being powered from the unregulated VCC rail instead of +5V, and the LM1117 output capacitor C2 is undersized for stability.\"}",
